[COMMENTS]
STATION,Flat-V weir. Holme Bridge reservoir group in the headwaters affect flow regime. GENERAL: Flat-V weir, 11m wide, 1:10 cross-slope. STATION HYDROMETRY: Weir drowns at high flows. Gauged to within 40% of QMED and flow is well contained above this, however there is uncertainty in the magnitude of the highest flows beyond the modular limit. No known by-passing. FLOW REGIME: Reservoirs in headwaters - compensation releases from Holme Bridge group affects flow regime. Net export of water from the catchment.
CATCHMENT,Predominantly Millstone Grit. Moorland headwaters; urban development and significant forest cover in the lower catchment.
Qmed Suitability,Only gauged to within 40% of QMED but flow is well contained and good consistency in gaugings so extrapolation to QMED seems reasonable.
Pooling Suitability,Not gauged to high enough level to give confidence in flows beyond modular limit of the weir.
[END]
